{
  "info": {
    "name": "DIKSHA IAM – New Contract (Phase 1 & 2)",
    "description": "## DIKSHA IAM Orchestrator – Complete API Test Suite\n\nTests all 11 OIDC endpoints implemented in Phase 1 & 2.\nSessions are maintained via **HttpOnly cookies** – Postman automatically stores & sends the `session_id` cookie.\n\n---\n\n### Flows covered\n\n**Flow A – Active user (Direct Grant)**\n1. `POST /iam/users/resolve` → confirm `ACTIVE` status\n2. `POST /iam/auth/login/init` → `flow:DIRECT_GRANT`, capture `txnId`\n3. `POST /iam/auth/login/password` → session cookie set, capture `sessionId`\n4. `GET /iam/users/me` → returns profile from session\n5. `POST /iam/auth/refresh` → rotates tokens\n6. `POST /iam/auth/logout` → clears cookie\n\n**Flow B – New/unactivated user (OTP → Keycloak activation)**\n1. `POST /iam/auth/login/init` → `flow:OTP_VERIFICATION`, capture `txnId`\n   *(or start from `POST /iam/password/setup/init` for explicit setup)*\n2. `POST /iam/password/setup/complete` → `authUrl` returned; open in browser to set password\n3. Browser follows `authUrl` → Keycloak sets password → redirects to `/auth/callback?code=&state=`\n4. `GET /iam/auth/callback?code=&state=` → session cookie set\n\n**Flow C – SSO (Google / State)**\n1. `GET /iam/sso/google/login` → `authUrl` returned; open in browser\n2. Provider → Orchestrator callback → sets cookie, redirects to `?sso_success=true`\n\n---\n\n### Environment Variables (set as collection variables or environment)\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `orchestratorUrl` | `http://localhost:4000` | IAM Orchestrator base URL |\n| `iamServiceUrl` | `http://localhost:3000` | IAM User Service base URL |\n| `testIdentifier` | `test@example.com` | Identifier to use in tests |\n| `testPassword` | `Test@1234` | Password for active user tests |\n| `txnId` | *(auto-set)* | Transaction ID from login/init |\n| `sessionId` | *(auto-set)* | Session ID from login/callback |\n| `authCode` | *(manual)* | Code from Keycloak callback URL |\n| `callbackState` | *(auto-set from setup)* | State from setup/complete |\n\n> **Tip**: Run requests in order within each folder.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "orchestratorUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "iamServiceUrl",   "value": "http://localhost:3000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "testIdentifier",  "value": "test@example.com",      "type": "string", "description": "Email/phone/username of the test user" },
    { "key": "testPassword",    "value": "Test@1234",             "type": "string", "description": "Password for active user (Flow A)" },
    { "key": "txnId",           "value": "",                      "type": "string", "description": "Auto-set by login/init or password/setup/init" },
    { "key": "sessionId",       "value": "",                      "type": "string", "description": "Auto-set by login/password or callback" },
    { "key": "authCode",        "value": "",                      "type": "string", "description": "Paste from Keycloak redirect URL (?code=...)" },
    { "key": "callbackState",   "value": "",                      "type": "string", "description": "Auto-set by password/setup/complete" },
    { "key": "accessToken",     "value": "",                      "type": "string", "description": "Auto-set after login" },
    { "key": "refreshToken",    "value": "",                      "type": "string", "description": "Auto-set after login" },
    { "key": "iamUserId",       "value": "",                      "type": "string", "description": "Auto-set after resolve or login" },
    { "key": "ssoProvider",     "value": "google",                "type": "string", "description": "SSO provider: google or state_<code>" }
  ],
  "item": [

    {
      "name": "🔵 Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] },
            "description": "Verify the orchestrator is running."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "bru.test('Body has status', () => {",
                  "  const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "  expect(b).to.have.property('status');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "🟢 Flow A – Active User (Direct Grant)",
      "description": "Full login/refresh/logout cycle for an already-activated user.\nRun requests top to bottom.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Resolve User",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{testIdentifier}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/users/resolve", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "users", "resolve"] },
            "description": "Resolve an identifier to the canonical user record.\nExpect `activationStatus: ACTIVE` for a user ready for direct grant."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has iamUserId', () => expect(b).to.have.property('iamUserId'));",
                  "bru.test('Has activationStatus', () => expect(b).to.have.property('activationStatus'));",
                  "if (b.iamUserId) bru.setVar('iamUserId', b.iamUserId);",
                  "console.log('activationStatus:', b.activationStatus);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Login Init",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{testIdentifier}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/auth/login/init", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "auth", "login", "init"] },
            "description": "Step 1 of login. Returns `flow: DIRECT_GRANT` for active users or `flow: OTP_VERIFICATION` for new users.\n\n**Expected for active user:** `{ flow: 'DIRECT_GRANT', txnId: '...' }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has flow', () => expect(b).to.have.property('flow'));",
                  "bru.test('Has txnId', () => expect(b).to.have.property('txnId'));",
                  "bru.setVar('txnId', b.txnId);",
                  "bru.test('Flow is DIRECT_GRANT', () => expect(b.flow).to.equal('DIRECT_GRANT'));",
                  "console.log('flow:', b.flow, '| txnId:', b.txnId);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Login Password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"txnId\": \"{{txnId}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{testPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/auth/login/password", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "auth", "login", "password"] },
            "description": "Step 2 of login (Direct Grant). Submits the password for the txnId obtained in Login Init.\n\nOn success: sets HttpOnly `session_id` cookie + returns `{ user, tokens, roles, sessionId, activationStatus }`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has sessionId', () => expect(b).to.have.property('sessionId'));",
                  "bru.test('Has user', () => expect(b).to.have.property('user'));",
                  "bru.test('Has tokens', () => expect(b).to.have.property('tokens'));",
                  "bru.test('activationStatus is ACTIVE', () => expect(b.activationStatus).to.equal('ACTIVE'));",
                  "if (b.sessionId) bru.setVar('sessionId', b.sessionId);",
                  "if (b.tokens?.accessToken)  bru.setVar('accessToken',  b.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "if (b.tokens?.refreshToken) bru.setVar('refreshToken', b.tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "if (b.user?.iamUserId || b.user?.id) bru.setVar('iamUserId', b.user.iamUserId || b.user.id);",
                  "console.log('sessionId:', b.sessionId, '| user:', b.user?.username);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Get Current User (session cookie)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/users/me", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "users", "me"] },
            "description": "Returns authenticated user profile from the session cookie.\n\nPostman automatically sends the `session_id` cookie set in step 3."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has iamUserId or id', () => expect(b.iamUserId || b.id).to.be.ok);",
                  "bru.test('activationStatus present', () => expect(b).to.have.property('activationStatus'));",
                  "console.log('me:', JSON.stringify(b, null, 2));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4b. Get Current User (Bearer token fallback)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/users/me", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "users", "me"] },
            "description": "Same as above but uses Bearer token in Authorization header instead of cookie.\nUseful for API-only clients."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200 or 401', () => {",
                  "  expect(bru.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 401]);",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('response:', bru.getBody());"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Refresh Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/auth/refresh", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "auth", "refresh"] },
            "description": "Refresh the access token. Can be called with:\n- Session cookie only (no body needed — orchestrator reads refresh token from session)\n- OR `refreshToken` in request body\n\nOn success: rotates session, updates cookie TTL, returns new tokens."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has accessToken', () => expect(b).to.have.property('accessToken'));",
                  "if (b.accessToken)  bru.setVar('accessToken',  b.accessToken);",
                  "if (b.refreshToken) bru.setVar('refreshToken', b.refreshToken);",
                  "console.log('New accessToken (first 40):', b.accessToken?.substring(0, 40));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\",\n  \"iamUserId\": \"{{iamUserId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/auth/logout", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "auth", "logout"] },
            "description": "Revokes the refresh token with Keycloak, deletes the server-side session, and clears the `session_id` cookie.\n\nAfter this, calling `/iam/users/me` should return 401."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('status is logged_out', () => expect(b.status).to.equal('logged_out'));",
                  "bru.setVar('accessToken', '');",
                  "bru.setVar('refreshToken', '');",
                  "bru.setVar('sessionId', '');",
                  "console.log('Logged out:', b);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6b. Verify Logout (should 401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/users/me", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "users", "me"] },
            "description": "After logout, the session cookie is cleared. Calling /iam/users/me should now return 401."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 401 (session cleared)', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(401));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "🟡 Flow B – New User (OTP → Password Setup → Activation)",
      "description": "Full onboarding flow for a user who hasn't set a password yet.\n\n1. Login init → OTP_VERIFICATION\n2. Password setup init → OTP sent\n3. Password setup complete → authUrl returned\n4. **Manual step**: Open authUrl in browser, set password, copy `code` + `state` from callback URL\n5. GET /iam/auth/callback?code=&state= → session established",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Login Init (new user)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{testIdentifier}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/auth/login/init", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "auth", "login", "init"] },
            "description": "For a new/unactivated user, flow is `OTP_VERIFICATION`.\nThe txnId is used in step 3."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has flow', () => expect(b).to.have.property('flow'));",
                  "bru.test('Has txnId', () => expect(b).to.have.property('txnId'));",
                  "bru.setVar('txnId', b.txnId);",
                  "console.log('flow:', b.flow, '| txnId:', b.txnId);",
                  "if (b.flow === 'DIRECT_GRANT') {",
                  "  console.warn('⚠️  User is already ACTIVE – use Flow A instead');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Password Setup Init (explicit – sends OTP)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{testIdentifier}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/password/setup/init", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "password", "setup", "init"] },
            "description": "Explicitly initiate password setup for a new/unactivated user.\nSends an OTP to the user's registered email/phone.\n\nReturns `{ flow: 'PASSWORD_SETUP', txnId, otpResponse }`.\n\nNote: You can also use this endpoint directly without going through login/init first."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has flow PASSWORD_SETUP', () => expect(b.flow).to.equal('PASSWORD_SETUP'));",
                  "bru.test('Has txnId', () => expect(b).to.have.property('txnId'));",
                  "bru.setVar('txnId', b.txnId);",
                  "console.log('txnId:', b.txnId, '| otpResponse:', JSON.stringify(b.otpResponse));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Password Setup Complete (verify OTP)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"txnId\": \"{{txnId}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"123456\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/password/setup/complete", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "password", "setup", "complete"] },
            "description": "Verify the OTP to complete the setup phase.\n\nReturns `{ flow: 'ACTIVATION_REQUIRED', authUrl, state, codeChallenge }`.\n\n**Next step (manual):**\n1. Copy `authUrl` from response\n2. Open it in a browser\n3. Keycloak shows the set-password form\n4. After setting password, browser is redirected to `/auth/callback?code=XXX&state=YYY`\n5. Copy `code` and `state` from the URL → paste into variables `authCode` and `callbackState`\n6. Run the next request ↓\n\n> If `USE_MOCK_OTP=true`, use `123456` as OTP."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has flow ACTIVATION_REQUIRED', () => expect(b.flow).to.equal('ACTIVATION_REQUIRED'));",
                  "bru.test('Has authUrl', () => expect(b).to.have.property('authUrl'));",
                  "bru.test('Has state', () => expect(b).to.have.property('state'));",
                  "bru.setVar('callbackState', b.state);",
                  "console.log('✅ Open this URL in a browser to set password:');",
                  "console.log(b.authUrl);",
                  "console.log('state saved:', b.state);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Auth Callback (GET – after Keycloak redirect)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/auth/callback?code={{authCode}}&state={{callbackState}}",
              "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"],
              "path": ["iam", "auth", "callback"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "code",  "value": "{{authCode}}",      "description": "Paste from Keycloak redirect URL" },
                { "key": "state", "value": "{{callbackState}}", "description": "Auto-set from step 3" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchange the authorization code with Keycloak.\n\n**Before running:**\n1. Set `authCode` collection variable to the `code` value from the browser redirect URL\n2. `callbackState` was auto-set in step 3\n\nOn success: sets HttpOnly `session_id` cookie and returns full session context."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has sessionId', () => expect(b).to.have.property('sessionId'));",
                  "bru.test('Has user', () => expect(b).to.have.property('user'));",
                  "bru.test('Has tokens', () => expect(b).to.have.property('tokens'));",
                  "if (b.sessionId) bru.setVar('sessionId', b.sessionId);",
                  "if (b.tokens?.accessToken)  bru.setVar('accessToken',  b.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "if (b.tokens?.refreshToken) bru.setVar('refreshToken', b.tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "console.log('Session established. sessionId:', b.sessionId, '| user:', b.user?.username);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4b. Auth Callback (POST – legacy)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"{{authCode}}\",\n  \"state\": \"{{callbackState}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/auth/callback", "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"], "path": ["iam", "auth", "callback"] },
            "description": "Legacy POST variant of the callback (code + state in request body instead of query params).\nSame behavior as the GET version."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has sessionId', () => expect(b).to.have.property('sessionId'));",
                  "if (b.sessionId) bru.setVar('sessionId', b.sessionId);",
                  "if (b.tokens?.accessToken)  bru.setVar('accessToken',  b.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "if (b.tokens?.refreshToken) bru.setVar('refreshToken', b.tokens.refreshToken);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "🟣 Flow C – SSO Login",
      "description": "SSO login via Google or State provider.\n\nBecause the SSO flow requires browser redirects, this folder documents the API endpoints involved and lets you inspect the `authUrl`.\n\nThe orchestrator callback sets the session cookie and redirects the browser to `?sso_success=true`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. SSO Login Init – Google",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/sso/google/login",
              "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"],
              "path": ["iam", "sso", "google", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Returns `{ authUrl, state }` for Google OAuth2 login.\n\nNext steps (browser-only):\n1. Copy `authUrl` from response\n2. Open in browser → authenticate with Google\n3. Browser is redirected back to `<frontend>/auth/callback?sso_success=true`\n4. Session cookie is set automatically"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.equal(200));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "bru.test('Has authUrl', () => expect(b).to.have.property('authUrl'));",
                  "bru.test('Has state', () => expect(b).to.have.property('state'));",
                  "bru.setVar('callbackState', b.state);",
                  "console.log('Google authUrl:', b.authUrl);",
                  "console.log('state:', b.state);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "1b. SSO Login Init – State (Meghalaya example)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{orchestratorUrl}}/iam/sso/state_meghalaya/login",
              "host": ["{{orchestratorUrl}}"],
              "path": ["iam", "sso", "state_meghalaya", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Returns `{ authUrl, state }` for State SSO (Meghalaya in this example).\nChange the provider segment to match your configured state code."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "bru.test('Status 200 or 400', () => expect(bru.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 400]));",
                  "const b = bru.getBody();",
                  "console.log(b);"
                ],
